From c38e6d9f351c5f2697bdb95b4ae2562d6a41cbbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Polli Harness Patch <patch@example.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 03:32:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] polli harness openclaw: single Pollinations setup path for
 OpenClaw

Adds `polli harness openclaw` alongside the existing DeepSeek Harness
integration, following the same on/off/status contract:

- `on` mints OpenClaw a dedicated Pollinations key (via the existing
  harness login/key flow), and either runs OpenClaw's own non-interactive
  onboarding (fresh install) or edits the existing openclaw.json in place.
- The pollinations provider's model list comes from the live
  gen.pollinations.ai/v1/models catalog (fetchHarnessModels), so there is
  no second hardcoded model registry to fall out of sync -- this is the
  same helper the dsh harness already uses.
- If the openclaw binary is missing, `on` stops and prints the official
  installer instead of guessing at one.
- `status` reports whether the provider, default model, key, and Polli
  skill are all in place.
- `off` restores the exact config/skill files from before `on` ran when
  nothing else has touched them since, or otherwise strips only the
  pollinations provider, the pollinations/* default model, and the Polli
  skill, leaving unrelated config (channels, other providers, workspace)
  untouched.

The old apps/openclaw/setup-pollinations.sh hardcoded a 9-model list
(pollinations/pollinations#8595) and had no revert path. It is now a
thin backward-compatible shim that forwards to `polli harness openclaw
on`; the README documents the new command as the primary path and keeps
a manual-JSON fallback for people who don't want to run the CLI.

CODING_HARNESSES.md (embedded verbatim into the Scalar docs at
gen.pollinations.ai/docs) documents on/off/status, model selection, the
missing-binary and fresh-install behavior, and what off does and does
not touch.

Tested: full polli-cli vitest suite (43/43) and tsup build pass; added
openclaw.test.ts (config/snapshot/restore logic, mirroring dsh.test.ts)
and openclaw.onboarding.test.ts (mocked-CLI coverage for the
missing-binary and fresh-install-bootstrap paths). Also manually
smoke-tested the built CLI end-to-end against a fake openclaw binary
and a fake Pollinations API server: fresh-install bootstrap preserves
the onboarded workspace/gateway/channels, on/status/off round-trip
correctly, and off-after-unrelated-edit strips only Pollinations keys.
